## 1. Installation & Permissions

AutoWifi interacts deeply with Android's network virtualization and hardware adapters. Upon launching the app for the first time, you will be prompted through an onboarding flow to grant the following permissions:

| Permission | Android Level | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Location (`ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION`)** | All | Required by Android to read Wi-Fi SSIDs, BSSIDs, and signal levels. *(AutoWifi does NOT track or store your physical GPS location).* |
| **Nearby Wi-Fi Devices (`NEARBY_WIFI_DEVICES`)** | Android 12+ | Allows scanning and discovering local Wi-Fi networks without accessing coarse GPS data. |
| **Notifications (`POST_NOTIFICATIONS`)** | Android 13+ | Displays the persistent foreground service notification showing live transfer speeds, IP status, and connection states. |
| **VPN Service (`BIND_VPN_SERVICE`)** | All | Prompts system VPN confirmation dialog when running in VPN mode to route traffic through the virtual TUN adapter. |
| **Query All Packages (`QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES`)** | Android 11+ | Enables the App-Split picker to populate all installed apps, services, and add-ons so you can choose which apps route through Wi-Fi. |
| **Biometrics (`USE_BIOMETRIC`)** | All | Protects masked passwords (Wi-Fi and SSH) and profile edits with your fingerprint or face recognition. |

