## 5. The Reverse Hotspot Guide

The **Reverse Hotspot** is a unique feature that lets you share your cellular data with another device without turning on your phone's hotspot:

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      Friend's Phone                    │
│  1. Turns on Mobile Hotspot (SSID: FriendWifi)         │
│  2. Installs & opens 'tun2socks' from Play Store       │
│  3. Sets Proxy Type: SOCKS5                            │
│  4. Sets Proxy Server: <Your AutoWifi IP> (e.g. 192.168.43.50) │
│  5. Sets Proxy Port: 9999                              │
│  6. Taps Connect in tun2socks                          │
└───────────────────────────▲────────────────────────────┘
                            │ Wi-Fi Connection
┌───────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────┐
│                       Your Phone                       │
│  1. Open AutoWifi                                      │
│  2. SSID: FriendWifi (Friend's hotspot password)       │
│  3. Go to Settings > SOCKS Routing > Select "Cellular" │
│  4. Select SOCKS Mode and tap Start                    │
│  5. Note the Wi-Fi IP displayed in yellow/green        │
└───────────────────────────▲────────────────────────────┘
                            │ Mobile Data
                     4G / 5G Internet
```

