## 8. Troubleshooting & FAQs

### Q: Why does AutoWifi show "SSID is empty"?
**A**: In Wi-Fi Mode, AutoWifi requires a valid SSID to connect to. Enter your Wi-Fi name or tap the Wi-Fi icon next to the field to select from nearby scanned networks.

### Q: Can AutoWifi connect to open (password-free) Wi-Fi networks?
**A**: Yes. In Version 1.0.7+, leave the Wi-Fi password field blank. AutoWifi automatically detects that the network has no security encryption and connects without throwing an error.

### Q: Why does the screen scroll when I tap Edit Profile?
**A**: Tapping the Edit icon automatically centers the input card above your software keyboard so all fields and buttons remain fully visible and accessible without being occluded by the keyboard.

### Q: Why does tapping outside lock the fields?
**A**: AutoWifi protects against accidental credential modifications. Tapping outside the active edit rectangle safely locks all fields and restores saved profile parameters. To save your changes permanently, tap the **Save** button.

### Q: How do I avoid high battery drain?
**A**: VPN App-Split and SOCKS modes are highly optimized using native socket relays. However, keeping dual active transmitters (Cellular + Wi-Fi) active simultaneously naturally uses more power than a single radio. It is recommended to use AutoWifi while connected to power if streaming heavily.
